cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your academic research, please cite it as below."
title: "AFRT Core: Standalone Computational Algorithms for Academic Workload Allocation and Cohort Partitioning"
authors:
  - family-names: "AFRT Research Team"
    given-names: "Computational Core"
    affiliation: "Tashkent State University of Economics"
abstract: >-
  AFRT Core is an open-access, decoupled computational research software package
  implementing deterministic algorithms for higher education academic workload
  calculation, cohort stream pooling, faculty quota validation, and timetable
  discrepancy reconciliation.
version: 0.1.0-alpha
date-released: "2026-10-23"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23611473
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23611473"
repository-code: "https://github.com/musobekgtd-stack/afrt-core"
keywords:
  - academic-workload
  - higher-education-management
  - cohort-bundling
  - curriculum-analytics
  - faculty-resource-tracking
